WEBVTT

00:13.280 --> 00:14.740
<i>Now's our chance!</i>

00:14.740 --> 00:17.030
<i>Love Cure Cure!</i>

00:17.030 --> 00:18.700
<i>I'll send you to eternal sleep!</i>

00:18.700 --> 00:24.200
<i>Marvelous Pretty Love and
Peace Death Explosion!</i>

00:19.670 --> 00:22.110
Oh, leveled up again!

00:24.940 --> 00:27.000
Oh right! An attendant!

00:27.320 --> 00:28.590
Attendant?

00:28.750 --> 00:29.670
<b>Whoops</b>

00:34.160 --> 00:36.480
Oh, just talking to myself.

00:36.480 --> 00:38.250
I'm going out for a walk.

01:00.490 --> 01:03.870
<b>Am I Actually the Strongest?</b>

02:13.570 --> 02:20.410
m 0 0 l 50 0 l 45 13 l -5 13

02:13.570 --> 02:20.410
Episode 6

02:13.570 --> 02:20.410
<b>I Need to Find an Attendant...!</b>

02:17.160 --> 02:19.180
<i>That was close.</i>

02:19.180 --> 02:22.530
<i>I almost slipped and mentioned 
the attendant in front of them.</i>

02:24.290 --> 02:26.310
<i>I still have three months to look,</i>

02:26.310 --> 02:28.950
<i>but who could I possibly find 
that's right for the job?</i>

02:30.620 --> 02:33.840
<i>Oh, yeah, if I go this way...</i>

02:54.160 --> 02:56.120
<i>That's right.</i>

02:56.120 --> 02:59.230
<i>It's a habitat for skeletons now.</i>

02:59.230 --> 03:02.100
Yes, those building materials go there.

03:02.100 --> 03:03.070
Oh?

03:05.250 --> 03:07.450
Why, is that my liege I see?

03:08.280 --> 03:10.790
I offer you my warmest welcome!

03:10.960 --> 03:12.040
<b>Salute!</b>

03:18.710 --> 03:21.500
<i>The Boney Army here is made up of skeletons</i>

03:21.500 --> 03:25.300
<i>who were called here by the summoners 
I defeated five years ago.</i>

03:25.740 --> 03:29.570
<i>For whatever reason, they started 
following me after that.</i>

03:29.570 --> 03:33.780
<i>So I gave them some land, and they 
ended up settling down.</i>

03:36.320 --> 03:41.130
I am delighted to see that you've 
made the long journey here.

03:41.130 --> 03:42.740
Oh, thanks.

03:42.990 --> 03:44.460
<i>This is Johnny,</i>

03:44.460 --> 03:47.480
<i>the capable commander of the Boney Army.</i>

03:47.910 --> 03:51.450
If you need anything of me, 
I am at your command.

03:51.450 --> 03:54.960
Oh, well, it's not a command or anything...

03:55.590 --> 03:58.160
but why are there other monsters here?

03:58.900 --> 04:02.030
They are stray monsters 
with nowhere else to go.

04:02.030 --> 04:04.200
Miss Flay has rounded them 
up throughout the province.

04:04.200 --> 04:05.830
<i>That's news to me!</i>

04:05.830 --> 04:11.580
Rest assured, they are all properly 
sequestered, and follow my directions.

04:11.890 --> 04:15.940
<i>On that note, I don't remember this 
district being here last time I was here.</i>

04:16.320 --> 04:18.030
<i>This place has really expanded.</i>

04:18.680 --> 04:23.820
<i>Well, if the monsters in our 
province are behaving here...</i>

04:23.820 --> 04:24.890
<i>Guess that's fine.</i>

04:25.200 --> 04:29.660
Since you're here, would you like to 
visit the other districts, as well?

04:29.660 --> 04:31.260
Huh? There's more?

04:32.920 --> 04:37.120
Here, we grow the crops 
that serve as our food.

04:37.120 --> 04:38.040
Huh...

04:38.040 --> 04:42.370
Throughout the year, we plant different 
crops on a seasonal basis,

04:42.370 --> 04:45.480
and cultivate those that will preserve well.

04:42.590 --> 04:47.640
Blah blah blah blah

04:46.020 --> 04:47.630
I see.

04:51.190 --> 04:53.380
Why, look at this!

04:53.380 --> 04:56.530
We failed to grow these last year, 
and now there's so much!

04:56.530 --> 04:58.640
<i>You guys did all this?!</i>

04:59.340 --> 05:03.570
Now we won't have to worry 
about food this winter!

05:03.790 --> 05:06.310
<i>You're not the ones eating this, right?</i>

05:06.310 --> 05:08.710
<i>So this is all for the monsters?</i>

05:08.710 --> 05:10.410
<i>How selfless!</i>

05:10.410 --> 05:13.650
We'll be able to house additional 
monsters with all of this.

05:10.410 --> 05:13.660
<b>Excited</b>

05:13.650 --> 05:16.210
<i>You're gonna take in even more of them?!</i>

05:17.130 --> 05:19.220
Blah, blah, blah... blah, blah, blah.

05:19.220 --> 05:22.170
Blah, blah... blah, blah, blah...

05:22.170 --> 05:24.210
Blah, blah, blah, blah!

05:24.210 --> 05:27.500
Blah, blah, blah... blah, blah, blah, blah.

05:27.900 --> 05:29.610
<i>A polite demeanor.</i>

05:29.610 --> 05:31.090
<i>Kind and fastidious.</i>

05:31.090 --> 05:34.090
<i>Respected by all, and highly loyal to me.</i>

05:34.090 --> 05:35.690
<i>Well versed in etiquette, too.</i>

05:36.090 --> 05:39.060
<i>What's more, his deep voice 
is music to my ears.</i>

05:39.670 --> 05:44.020
<i>If I added on some flesh, I could probably 
make him look pretty much like a human.</i>

05:44.020 --> 05:46.940
<i>Could I have found the perfect attendant?</i>

05:46.940 --> 05:49.900
In the future, we hope to increase 
production of grain and other feed,

05:49.900 --> 05:52.090
thus allowing us to keep more livestock,

05:50.120 --> 05:54.660
<b>Blah blah blah</b>

05:52.090 --> 05:55.990
but that'll depend on how the western 
district development progresses.

05:54.700 --> 06:03.550
<b>Blah blah blah</b>

05:55.990 --> 05:57.880
With that in mind, we still 
face a number of obstacles

05:57.880 --> 05:59.700
and, at present, find ourselves 
struggling to make headway,

05:59.700 --> 06:03.540
but considering the increase of 
monsters, I believe we can all...

06:02.140 --> 06:03.540
<i>He talks too much!</i>

06:03.540 --> 06:06.610
<i>That's right. He's so talkative.</i>

06:03.550 --> 06:10.390
<b>Blah blah blah</b>

06:06.610 --> 06:09.920
<i>If I had to listen to this everyday, 
frankly, I'd go insane!</i>

06:10.380 --> 06:11.610
<i>So close!</i>

06:11.610 --> 06:13.840
<i>It really is a shame...</i>

06:13.840 --> 06:17.670
Oh? You have a troubled look on your face.

06:17.670 --> 06:20.020
Have I acted in error in some way?

06:20.020 --> 06:21.810
Oh, no.

06:21.810 --> 06:25.060
I was just impressed at how 
well you've been doing.

06:25.450 --> 06:27.480
Oh, I don't deserve such praise!

06:27.480 --> 06:28.960
I can feel it in my bones!

06:29.370 --> 06:33.700
My liege, I will continue to work 
myself to the bone for you!

06:34.130 --> 06:35.840
Just a little skeleton joke!

06:37.770 --> 06:40.920
<i>Man, and he really is such 
a nice, honest guy!</i>

06:41.440 --> 06:43.950
Now, then, let me take you to our next stop.

06:43.950 --> 06:47.140
Oh, I've got other business after this.

06:47.140 --> 06:49.480
I see. What a shame.

06:56.140 --> 06:57.500
<i>I'm beat.</i>

06:58.060 --> 07:02.230
<i>I thought I could relax by myself out here.</i>

07:02.230 --> 07:06.520
<i>But before I knew it, 
it turned into a monster paradise!</i>

07:06.520 --> 07:09.970
<i>How come nothing ever works out for me?</i>

07:17.020 --> 07:20.840
<i>Right. I forgot you were here, too.</i>

07:22.250 --> 07:27.760
<i>This is Gigan, the Gigant Golem also 
called here by those summoners.</i>

07:37.980 --> 07:39.130
For me?

07:42.640 --> 07:45.360
Because... it was pretty.

07:45.360 --> 07:46.540
<i>A maiden of pure heart?!</i>

07:46.540 --> 07:48.790
<i>Wait, that's what you sound like?</i>

07:49.550 --> 07:50.680
Thanks.

07:51.860 --> 07:54.660
<i>Gigan is a lot gentler than it looks.</i>

07:55.090 --> 07:59.550
<i>It never gets in my way, so you 
could say it'd be a good attendant.</i>

08:00.730 --> 08:02.220
<i>But it's huge.</i>

08:02.820 --> 08:06.350
<i>Oh, yeah, and it's always all by itself...</i>

08:06.350 --> 08:07.750
<i>I hope it's okay.</i>

08:08.180 --> 08:11.170
Could it be, you don't like 
being in the village?

08:13.130 --> 08:15.870
I... love...

08:15.870 --> 08:18.620
Oh, you love this spot, huh?

08:18.620 --> 08:19.540
That's good to hear.

08:21.190 --> 08:23.270
Love... Master.

08:23.270 --> 08:24.300
<i>You meant me?!</i>

08:30.960 --> 08:33.610
<i>I just can't seem to find anyone.</i>

08:35.950 --> 08:36.640
<i>Huh?</i>

08:37.100 --> 08:40.840
<i>Could it be that picking out an attendant 
is actually a lot of hard work?</i>

08:42.070 --> 08:43.740
<i>Let's go back for now.</i>

08:48.400 --> 08:49.770
My master.

08:49.770 --> 08:53.520
What was this "attendant" 
you mentioned before?

08:54.300 --> 08:59.510
<b>Staaaare</b>

08:54.760 --> 08:59.150
<i>How come she's only sharp-witted 
at times like these?</i>

08:59.500 --> 09:01.930
<i>More like, can I just pick Flay?</i>

09:01.930 --> 09:03.920
You can't take Flay.

09:03.920 --> 09:05.050
Can't take Flay...

09:05.350 --> 09:06.450
Can't take Flay...

09:06.680 --> 09:07.730
Can't take Flay...

09:08.070 --> 09:09.570
It's got nothing to do with you!

09:11.770 --> 09:15.860
M-Master!

09:11.780 --> 09:15.860
<b>Skedaddle</b>

09:18.060 --> 09:19.400
Haruto.

09:19.400 --> 09:23.750
I've come up with a suitable reading 
for the Black Knight's name.

09:23.750 --> 09:24.410
Huh?

09:26.970 --> 09:30.500
Schwarze Krieger. Or Shiva for short.

09:30.500 --> 09:32.090
<i>What is that, German?</i>

09:32.090 --> 09:34.440
I looked it up on the Internet!

09:34.440 --> 09:38.430
It's the name of a supreme deity that 
reigns over destruction and creation!

09:38.430 --> 09:40.870
I thought it'd be perfect for you!

09:40.870 --> 09:45.250
<i>I'm so sorry for turning a young noblewoman 
from a fantasy world into this!</i>

09:45.640 --> 09:57.450
<b>Blah blah blah</b>

09:45.650 --> 09:47.890
Welcome, Lady Charlotte.

09:47.890 --> 09:50.510
I've heard all about you from Miss Flay.

09:50.510 --> 09:53.200
This is a place for those 
who were saved by my liege,

09:53.200 --> 09:57.430
as well as a shelter for the stray 
monsters rounded up by Miss Flay.

09:57.740 --> 09:59.720
Wow, Haruto!

09:59.720 --> 10:03.210
You found a place for all 
these monsters to live?

10:01.700 --> 10:03.200
<b>Mostly her work</b>

10:03.440 --> 10:07.190
I've come up with a suitable 
name for this place.

10:08.640 --> 10:11.660
How does Pandemonium sound?

10:11.960 --> 10:14.670
m 0 0 l 180 0 l 180 64 l 0 64

10:11.960 --> 10:14.670
New name:
<b>Pandemonium
</b>The Garden of Demons

10:15.300 --> 10:16.870
Magnificent.

10:21.600 --> 10:22.930
<b>Am I Actually the Strongest?</b>

10:44.440 --> 10:46.330
We've finally tracked it down.

10:46.890 --> 10:49.440
Look at the size of this Blizzard Dragon!

10:49.790 --> 10:52.410
We'll be in for a fat bounty 
if we slay this thing.

10:58.050 --> 10:59.220
It disappeared?!

11:01.410 --> 11:02.360
Above us!

11:06.300 --> 11:07.510
What are you doing?!

11:07.510 --> 11:08.810
After it, quick!

11:08.810 --> 11:10.830
You're gonna let it get away!

11:43.510 --> 11:44.390
What?

11:44.390 --> 11:48.220
A large blue dragon near the 
border we share with the Empire?

11:48.220 --> 11:49.370
Yeah.

11:49.370 --> 11:51.310
It flew this way from the Empire,

11:51.310 --> 11:54.100
but it dropped out of the sky before 
it reached our kingdom's borders.

11:54.430 --> 11:56.420
So it's not in our province, then.

11:56.420 --> 11:58.990
Which means it's none of our business.

11:59.250 --> 12:00.590
You could say that.

12:00.590 --> 12:04.060
However, it might show itself 
again and enter our territory.

12:04.400 --> 12:08.020
The dragon was most likely wounded 
in a hunt within imperial borders.

12:08.020 --> 12:10.700
So if it does just happen 
to go on a rampage,

12:10.700 --> 12:13.110
it would cause the loss of 
a great number of lives.

12:13.440 --> 12:14.540
And that's why...

12:15.540 --> 12:19.120
I'd like Flay, as a demon, 
to go scope out the situation.

12:19.120 --> 12:20.380
I refuse!

12:20.380 --> 12:22.870
I only obey Lord Haruto's commands!

12:23.170 --> 12:25.720
Then think of it as an order from me.

12:27.650 --> 12:29.440
<i>So much for obeying me!</i>

12:31.190 --> 12:32.900
Is there a reason you won't?

12:33.230 --> 12:38.360
A dragon that large couldn't have 
been born in the past several years.

12:38.650 --> 12:41.320
However, I know of no blue dragons.

12:41.320 --> 12:45.440
Which means that while we demons were 
desperately waging war against humans,

12:45.440 --> 12:48.760
it must have been hiding away in 
the mountains, feigning ignorance.

12:50.340 --> 12:53.630
I see no reason to offer safe 
harbor to someone so cowardly.

12:53.630 --> 12:54.890
<i>I see.</i>

12:54.890 --> 12:57.840
<i>This is a very deep-rooted issue for Flay.</i>

13:00.040 --> 13:02.540
Can you give me some time 
to think about this?

13:02.540 --> 13:03.640
Sure.

13:03.640 --> 13:06.210
Time is of the essence, though.

13:06.210 --> 13:07.170
Got it.

13:13.950 --> 13:16.620
You shouldn't eavesdrop, Char.

13:17.120 --> 13:20.830
Um, well... I'm sorry.

13:22.190 --> 13:26.450
Flay, can't you help that dragon out?

13:26.450 --> 13:30.940
I'm sure it must feel so helpless, 
all alone and wounded!

13:30.940 --> 13:33.060
G-Grr...

13:34.760 --> 13:36.950
Well, you heard her.

13:36.950 --> 13:40.080
A request from Char is a request from me.

13:40.520 --> 13:43.810
I suppose I must, if you so insist.

13:44.230 --> 13:46.720
Let's go and wipe out those 
no-good adventurers!

13:46.720 --> 13:48.310
That's not what I said.

13:57.390 --> 13:59.180
Oh, found it.

13:59.180 --> 14:02.550
<i>Huh, so this is what dragons 
look like in this world.</i>

14:02.550 --> 14:05.390
<i>It looks like it's in really bad shape.</i>

14:05.910 --> 14:07.280
Lord Haruto.

14:12.010 --> 14:14.660
<i>Looks like we've got no time to spare.</i>

14:14.660 --> 14:15.760
Let's go.

14:15.760 --> 14:16.610
Yes!

14:25.760 --> 14:27.000
I found it!

14:30.450 --> 14:32.090
You're not getting away this time!

14:32.090 --> 14:33.480
Let's take it out all at once!

14:41.980 --> 14:44.730
The Black Knight has arrived!

14:45.000 --> 14:46.390
Rejuvenate!

14:48.290 --> 14:51.130
Wh-Where did they come from?

14:51.720 --> 14:53.500
You worthless scoundrels.

14:53.500 --> 14:56.750
Ganging up on and torturing the weak!

14:56.750 --> 14:59.810
I'll reduce you all to ashes!

14:59.810 --> 15:00.450
Ah.

15:00.450 --> 15:02.880
Burn to death!

15:04.900 --> 15:06.650
Hey, calm down!

15:06.650 --> 15:08.480
Stay, stay!

15:18.910 --> 15:20.260
Hello there.

15:20.260 --> 15:23.430
I'm the Black Knight, hero of justice...

15:28.190 --> 15:29.740
How dare you?!

15:29.740 --> 15:31.530
Show my master some respect!

15:33.740 --> 15:35.140
It's fine.

15:35.140 --> 15:38.140
I'm sure you've been on edge,
 with those adventurers after you.

15:38.140 --> 15:39.790
I don't mind at all.

15:40.250 --> 15:41.850
Did you think I'd say that?!

15:40.250 --> 15:46.630
<b>Peeved</b>

15:41.850 --> 15:43.800
I came all this way to help you!

15:43.800 --> 15:46.630
I'll unheal those wounds 
if you do that again!

15:46.630 --> 15:49.170
Help me? You did?

15:49.170 --> 15:53.110
<i>Oh, I can hear her voice 
directly in my head.</i>

15:53.110 --> 15:54.640
<i>Flay did that, too.</i>

15:54.640 --> 15:56.840
It looks like you can speak, 
so let me ask this.

15:57.220 --> 15:58.570
Who, exactly, are you?

16:02.740 --> 16:04.920
You're a demon, aren't you?

16:04.920 --> 16:06.450
<i>Ignoring me, huh?</i>

16:06.450 --> 16:09.900
Hey, why is a demon like 
you obeying a human?

16:09.900 --> 16:11.390
Please tell me why.

16:13.920 --> 16:16.380
If you insist, I don't mind telling you...

16:16.740 --> 16:20.710
All about how great my master 
is and our fated encounter!

16:21.450 --> 16:23.670
<b>One Hour Later</b>

16:23.670 --> 16:25.250
That's how it is.

16:25.250 --> 16:27.250
Well? Amazing, right?

16:27.250 --> 16:29.450
Yeah, I get it now.

16:29.450 --> 16:32.350
Who could imagine the Demon 
King had reincarnated?

16:32.350 --> 16:34.800
<i>Oh, that backstory's still a thing, huh?</i>

16:34.800 --> 16:39.510
I'm sorry I didn't fight alongside 
the demons during the war.

16:39.830 --> 16:42.440
I don't like fighting.

16:42.970 --> 16:46.980
<i>I see. Guess even demons come 
in all shapes and sizes.</i>

16:47.370 --> 16:50.440
So until now, what were 
you up to, and where?

16:50.690 --> 16:55.640
I lived a quiet life deep in the 
mountains, hoping not to be noticed.

16:55.640 --> 16:57.420
For about 300 years.

16:57.420 --> 16:58.860
Three hundred years?!

16:58.860 --> 17:02.490
<i>Sh-She's a shut-in on a whole other scale!</i>

16:59.790 --> 17:02.500
<b>Wow</b>

17:01.040 --> 17:02.500
<b>Gaze of
jealousy</b>

17:02.490 --> 17:04.340
What did you do that whole time?!

17:04.340 --> 17:06.260
Tell me all about it!

17:06.760 --> 17:11.960
At first, I spent all my days just 
curled up deep inside a cave.

17:13.960 --> 17:19.250
But one day, an adventurer stayed 
the night and left a book behind.

17:19.910 --> 17:24.930
I read that book so many 
times, over... and over...

17:27.530 --> 17:29.640
I want to read more books.

17:30.160 --> 17:34.440
Before I knew it, I'd flown out of 
my cave and was headed toward town.

17:55.500 --> 17:58.930
And so, from time to time, in my human form,

17:58.930 --> 18:02.140
I'd go into human villages 
to take books back with me.

18:02.730 --> 18:06.730
I did this countless times 
and gained knowledge.

18:07.400 --> 18:09.020
It was so much fun...

18:10.190 --> 18:13.930
However, I was discovered by adventurers.

18:34.520 --> 18:35.990
That's what happened.

18:37.420 --> 18:42.130
Wh-What a pitiful tale!

18:42.130 --> 18:45.280
Chased out of your den, 
almost killed by pesky humans...

18:45.280 --> 18:47.480
It must have been so difficult for you!

18:48.010 --> 18:51.660
Okay, I acknowledge you as my brethren.

18:51.660 --> 18:53.980
I will permit you to enter Pandemonium.

18:53.980 --> 18:56.040
Huh? Where's that?

18:56.040 --> 18:58.430
It's your second home.

18:58.430 --> 18:59.790
Where'd the name come from?

18:59.790 --> 19:01.880
The young lady called it that.

19:01.880 --> 19:03.840
Is that so?

19:05.280 --> 19:09.350
Well, the reason we came here in the 
first place was to offer you shelter.

19:09.350 --> 19:11.300
Would you like to come with us?

19:11.300 --> 19:12.420
I'd be happy to.

19:12.760 --> 19:14.820
I learned of them through my books...

19:14.820 --> 19:16.540
Those things called feelings.

19:16.970 --> 19:22.950
Maybe what I wanted all along was to 
interact with others, just like this.

19:23.470 --> 19:26.490
That's right, I never did show my gratitude.

19:26.490 --> 19:29.480
Thank you for saving me earlier.

19:29.480 --> 19:32.280
I am a Blizzard Dragon.

19:32.280 --> 19:36.690
I will accept you as my master 
and give my life for you.

19:39.890 --> 19:42.750
<i>Th-This turn of events, could it be...?!</i>

20:00.480 --> 20:03.420
That's right. I know better, after Flay.

20:03.650 --> 20:06.590
It's not a catsuit like last time!

20:07.880 --> 20:09.840
Where did these clothes come from?

20:09.840 --> 20:11.230
Creation magic?

20:11.230 --> 20:13.980
Not understanding the logic behind 
something makes me so uneasy...

20:14.330 --> 20:17.330
Well, we can discuss that 
later, little by little.

20:18.130 --> 20:20.550
Let me reintroduce myself.

20:21.050 --> 20:22.920
My name is Haruto Zenfis.

20:22.920 --> 20:25.410
I'm the son of the margrave of 
the nearby border province.

20:25.410 --> 20:27.260
Um...

20:27.260 --> 20:30.760
I don't have my own name, 
so please give me one.

20:30.760 --> 20:31.810
Dragon.

20:32.200 --> 20:36.160
Blizzard... Lizard...

20:37.150 --> 20:38.690
How about Liza?

20:38.690 --> 20:40.170
Nice to meet you, Liza.

20:40.480 --> 20:41.590
Liza.

20:41.590 --> 20:43.410
Yeah, it has a nice ring to it.

20:43.830 --> 20:44.900
I like it.

20:45.440 --> 20:48.050
Nice to meet you, Lord Haruto.

20:53.000 --> 20:56.830
Liza, there's one thing I need you to know.

21:00.170 --> 21:03.520
I'm the one who first served Lord Haruto!

21:03.890 --> 21:06.520
And you're the second!

21:06.520 --> 21:08.600
You know what that means, don't you?

21:09.710 --> 21:10.540
Yeah.

21:11.900 --> 21:14.530
All right. For now, just follow me.

21:23.430 --> 21:25.010
I'd expect no less from a dragon.

21:25.010 --> 21:26.770
I see you can fly in this form, too.

21:27.220 --> 21:28.550
Let's go, then.

21:28.550 --> 21:29.330
Yeah.

21:34.420 --> 21:38.510
I won't lose to you!

